{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "Murder Is Game Over: The Blackinton Curse",
    "steam_appid": 3046150,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3046150/extras/aa9f2f0a72b191afc0cd1279ac070e39.avif?t=1745283712\" data-has-big width=800 height=204 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Following the death of a family matriarch, the surviving heirs return from abroad to their childhood home in The Berkshires. But in addition to the family\u2019s Victorian mansion, sprawling acreage, and millions of dollars, they\u2019ve also inherited something much more sinister. A spooky masked figure appears and warns the siblings that they will be the next victims of a grizzly family curse dating back to the Gilded Age. After another fatality on the property, the prophecy is seemingly proven true. Can you help Cleo and Detective Guy crack the mystery of multiple murders and a 150-year-old legend? </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Features </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- stand-alone murder mystery whodunit RPG</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- play as a detective and dog crime-solving team</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- explore the area and look for clues</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- interview suspects and make deductions</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- solve the case and apprehend the guilty</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- optional horror gameplay</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- new &quot;open world&quot; design.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3046150/extras/aa9f2f0a72b191afc0cd1279ac070e39.avif?t=1745283712\" data-has-big width=800 height=204 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Following the death of a family matriarch, the surviving heirs return from abroad to their childhood home in The Berkshires. But in addition to the family\u2019s Victorian mansion, sprawling acreage, and millions of dollars, they\u2019ve also inherited something much more sinister. A spooky masked figure appears and warns the siblings that they will be the next victims of a grizzly family curse dating back to the Gilded Age. After another fatality on the property, the prophecy is seemingly proven true. Can you help Cleo and Detective Guy crack the mystery of multiple murders and a 150-year-old legend? </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Features </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- stand-alone murder mystery whodunit RPG</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- play as a detective and dog crime-solving team</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- explore the area and look for clues</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- interview suspects and make deductions</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- solve the case and apprehend the guilty</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- optional horror gameplay</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- new &quot;open world&quot; design.</p>",
    "short_description": "A new stand-alone murder mystery in the Murder Is Game Over series. Can you break the 150-year-old family curse before it claims another victim?",
    "supported_languages": "English",
    "reviews": "\u201cIf you like whodunit games and have played other titles in the series, Murder Is Game Over: The Blackinton Curse is a must-have addition to your library. On the other hand, if you are new to the series, this is a great place to start.\u201d<br>85/100 \u2013 1 Up Nerd<br><br>\u201cThe game\u2019s true strength lies in a lovingly crafted, often ethereal atmosphere \u2014 well-defined and interesting visuals paired with a soundtrack that bounds between mellow, mysterious and malevolent at different turns.\u201d<br>The Berkshire Eagle<br><br>\u201cAs soon as I saw the cemetery scene I was hooked! It's super Scooby-tastic and it's great!\u201d<br>Scooby Addicts<br>",
